Package: stepFMR
Title: Finite Mixture Regression with Variable and Effect-Type Selection
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Tulio", "Martins", email = "tbatista@uoguelph.ca", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
      person("Jackson", "Mitchell", email = "jmitch19@uoguelph.ca", role = c("aut", "cph")),
      person("Zeny", "Feng", email = "zfeng@uoguelph.ca", role = c("ctb", "ths", "cph")),
      person("Allan", "Willms", email = "awillms@uoguelph.ca", role = c("ctb", "ths", "cph")),
      person("Chong", "Gan", email = "gan.c@queensu.ca", role = c("ctb")))
Description: Implements finite mixture regression models for Gaussian, Poisson,
    binomial, with procedures for selecting covariates and
    determining whether covariate effects are heterogeneous or homogeneous across
    mixture components. Estimation is performed using EM algorithms,
    with weighted least squares and structured QR decompositions for efficient matrix inversions
    in the M-step.
